Package: openBISG
Title: Open Bayesian Improved Surname Geocoding for Race, Hispanic-Origin
    and Sex Probabilities from 2020 U.S. Census Names
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R:
    person("openBISG", "contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "noreply@example.com")
Description: Lookup tables and a Naive-Bayes / BISG / BIFSG probability
    calculator built from the U.S. Census Bureau's 2020 Decennial Census
    frequently occurring first and last names tabulations, the
    2020-2024 ACS Citizen Voting Age Population (CVAP) Special
    Tabulation, and the 2020 P.L. 94-171 Redistricting Data. Given any
    combination of first name, last name, and a geography (ZIP / ZCTA,
    Census Tract, Block Group, or Census Block), returns the
    probability that the bearer belongs to each of six
    race/Hispanic-origin groups, plus a probability of sex from the
    first-name by-sex table. Includes a Shiny app that mirrors the
    bundled lookup page.
